Actually, I agree it would lead to too much abuse.  Anyone
familiar with nethack probably doesn't need to cheat to enjoy the
game, and newbies who do cheat aren't really becoming familiar
with nethack.
 
 A possible solution:  Set "BIRTHDAY" to the release date of that
particular version.  (Of course, it may have to go into the FAQ,
I can see it now:  "How come in version 3.x the birthday was
March 29th and in version 3.y the birthday is June 2?"  :)

>option.  And the moon phase thing.  If I always wanted to start out lucky, I
>could always set the clock to corrospond with the date of a full moon, but
>what good would that be?

Actually, on my home computer I don't bother loading in the clock
when I play nethack, so it reads the date from the last file
written to disk.  Since I keep nethack on it's own disks, usually
there isn't much change in the date.
 
Yes, I have started out lucky for a week straight.  Then I
thought about it and added 2 weeks to my date.  I tend to become
attached to my characters so much less that way.  :)
 
Besides, with the luckstone at the bottom of the mines now, it
usually isn't too critical what the moon's phase is, as opposed
to 3.0 when it was occasionally quite difficult to find that
wonderful luckstone.  (I seemed to find loadstones quite often,
but I think that was just bad luck.)
 
